    "created_at": "2017-04-21T05:29:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-21T05:29:55Z",
    "body": "> Even for postMessage()\r\n\r\nYou mean in terms of the `.origin` of the MessageEvent?  It's punycode in Chrome and Safari.\r\n\r\n> How is anyone writing reliable code for that then?\r\n\r\nAs long as you only expect messages from your own domain, you could compare to location.origin or something and it would work across all browsers.\r\n\r\nIf you expect messages from other hostnames, and they're IDN, then I expect people either don't check .origin or end up with code that only works in some browsers.  I'm not sure which is more likely.",
