    "created_at": "2017-04-21T10:03:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-21T10:03:53Z",
    "body": "I was going to write tests, but if Chrome and Safari indeed never expose Unicode origins I'm not sure what the point is since I don't know what the correct results should be.\r\n\r\n@foolip who can make a decision here on behalf of Chrome? @hober who can make a decision here on behalf of Safari? @travisleithead who can make a decision on behalf of Edge?\r\n\r\nIt seems pretty clear Firefox would favor ToUnicode, but if Firefox is alone that's not a tenable position. Though I do wonder what Firefox returns when mixed scripts are used within the same label. Does it return what the UI would display in that case (which I believe is Punycode) or what ToUnicode as defined at http://www.unicode.org/reports/tr46/#ToUnicode returns (which I believe is not Punycode)? If it's not always the latter than the Firefox solution seems a lot harder to get interoperable since we cannot really require UI even though it would be good here...",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
