    "body": "```\r\nSELECT * FROM (\r\nSELECT page, url, REGEXP_EXTRACT(body, r'(.{50}\\.origin\\s*!?===?\\s*[\"\\'][^\\)]+)') AS match\r\nFROM [httparchive:har.2017_03_15_chrome_requests_bodies]\r\n) WHERE match != \"null\"\r\nAND match CONTAINS \"xn--\"\r\nOR REGEXP_MATCH(match, r'[\\x80-\\xff]')\r\n```\r\nThis only brought up a single result, which was a false positive:\r\n```\r\n\t \r\n1\thttp://www.alienvault.com/\thttps://www.alienvault.com/cache/98e1630ea768312e0375124c2f1cf8fc795204c6.1489172110.js\tevent){ââif($('.vidyard_iframe').length&&event.origin==='https://play.vidyard.com'&&!setupVidyardDone\r\n```\r\n\r\nSearching github reveals existence proof of code expecting punycode (also in `Origin` request header?). I don't know if it's possible to search github for things expecting Unicode serialization...\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/search?utf8=✓&q=\"origin+https+xn\"+OR+\"origin+http+xn\"&type=Code",
