    "body": "> In w3c/web-platform-tests#5633 I fix self.origin test\r\n\r\nOuch.  I wrote a test for the IDN thing, and just messed it up.  :(\r\n\r\n> Though I do wonder what Firefox returns when mixed scripts are used within the same label. \r\n\r\nI don't have a testcase on hand, but code inspection suggests we're using http://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/7aa21f3b531ddee90a353215bd86e97d6974e25b/netwerk/dns/nsIIDNService.idl#51-57 and not http://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/7aa21f3b531ddee90a353215bd86e97d6974e25b/netwerk/dns/nsIIDNService.idl#32-38 which I agree is suboptimal.  We should probably change to a combination of http://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/7aa21f3b531ddee90a353215bd86e97d6974e25b/netwerk/dns/nsIIDNService.idl#25-29 and http://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/7aa21f3b531ddee90a353215bd86e97d6974e25b/netwerk/dns/nsIIDNService.idl#32-38\r\n",
