    "updated_at": "2017-04-24T13:35:12Z",
    "body": "Note that we also have tests for this in web-platform-tests here:\r\n\r\n* url/a-element-origin.html\r\n* url/a-element-origin-xhtml.xhtml\r\n* url/url-origin.html\r\n\r\nFirefox using its display algorithm is already accounted for by two tests:\r\n\r\n> assert_equals: origin expected \"ftp://☃\" but got \"ftp://xn--n3h\"\r\n> assert_equals: origin expected \"https://☃\" but got \"https://xn--n3h\"\r\n\r\nWe should probably add mixed-script tests, but deciding what to do here in general would be good as a first step.",
