    "created_at": "2017-05-11T00:04:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-11T00:04:24Z",
    "body": "> Though I do wonder what Firefox returns when mixed scripts are used within the same label.\r\n\r\nMixed scripts return punycode [1]. Also, it would always return punycode if you set the _network.IDN_show_punycode_ pref to true. I think it would be much more consistent to always return punycode for all our URL APIs, and optionally expose domainToUnicode to developers.\r\n\r\n[1] http://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/d66b9f27d5630a90b2fce4d70d4e9050f43df9b4/dom/tests/mochitest/dom-level0/test_setting_document.domain_idn.html#104\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
